C('8-012',[18],'J156-8-03','6-35','La donnée d’un magasin ensembliste ... M⊂Figel(L)','Set-theoretic magasins, up to isomorphism, are sets L and collections M of elementary set-theoretic figures closed under passage to the elementary subfigure at each stratum and containing every singleton point figure. The refinement and compatibility reflection conditions in lines 6–13 distinguish this from merely pre-set-theoretic magmas.','stated without proof','magasins')
C('8-013',[19,20],'J156-8-03','48-98','antifiltre ... contenant ... figures élémentaires ... figure vide','A chosen M-atlas is a nonempty lower subset of Fig(M), containing all elementary figures and closed under existing binary joins. It is {∅} iff M is empty. The elementary propositions restrict to any such atlas; arbitrary-cover gluing additionally requires At Fil: increasing refinements whose restrictions to each elementary face stabilize have a supremum in the atlas.','stated without proof','sheaf')
C('8-014',[20,21,22,23,24],'J156-8-03','101-283','Les deux pts de vue ... sont équivalents','Three presentations are asserted equivalent at the level of groupoids of structures: a magasin with chosen atlas; an atlas poset generated by completely join-irreducible figures with local compatibility/refinement axioms; and a separating incidence relation between elementary figures and all figures, each element having a least incident figure, with bounded-union and face-local axioms. Morphisms beyond isomorphisms are not defined by this equivalence.','proof sketched','order')
C('8-015',[23],'J156-8-03','230-252','toute partie fermée ... est dans ...','Under incidence separation, existence of least incident figures, and closure under bounded unions, every lower subset of a represented figure is represented: it is the bounded union of the principal figures of its elements. The induced specialization preorder is antisymmetric by separation.','proof sketched','order')
C('8-016',[24,25,26],'J156-8-03','285-353','Est-ce suffisant ? ... Mag 1 ... Mag 2','For a prepolyhedral magasin (two elements with common upper and lower bounds have a meet), define X≪polY by X≪Y and by every restriction X|Y′, Y′≤Y, being empty or elementary. Then (M,≤,≪pol,|°|) is again a magasin; carrier sets are unchanged where ≪pol holds, and ≪°pol is the conjunction of ≪pol with ≪°. The argument begun by the question on scan 25 is completed on scan 26; it is not an unresolved problem.','proved there','polyhedral')
C('8-017',[26,27,28,29],'J156-8-04','12-146','Figpol(M)⊊Fig(M) ... figure circulaire','A magasin is polyhedral iff ≪=≪pol. Even then, figures all of whose pairs of faces have empty or principal intersection form in general a proper subset of all figures: a circle split into two arcs has their two endpoints as a nonprincipal intersection. Polyhedral compatibility is inherited by faces; a union of two polyhedral figures exists iff every cross-pair of elementary faces is polyhedrally compatible. Atlas closure uses this stronger compatibility.','proof sketched','polyhedral')
C('8-018',[29,30,31],'J156-8-04','152-247','X≪Y ⇔ ∃Y′, X≪°Y′≤Y','An alternative primitive-data presentation uses two partial orders ≤ and ≪°, unique carriers, face lifting, and interior disjointness; general refinement is their relation composite. Carrier uniqueness and face lifting yield transitivity and recover the given open-refinement relation. However the new Mag4′ printed at line 247 only treats comparable distinct elements, whereas original Mag4 treated distinct faces of one element. The claimed full equivalence depends on resolving that weakening, separately from the doubtful negation in the transcription.','stated without proof','magasins',confidence='low')
C('8-019',[32,33],'J156-8-04','280-323','L={X ... minimal pour ≤ et pour ≪°}','In the alternative presentation, lieux are simultaneously minimal for ≤ and ≪°. For strictly divisible magasins disjointness is recovered by pairwise disjointness of interior lieux; in the quasi-set-theoretic case it becomes disjointness of interior shadows. The printed Mag div1–3 omit the previously essential nonemptiness condition, whereas Mag quens3 restores it. Thus this page is an axiom-reformulation draft, not an unconditional equivalence theorem.','stated without proof','magasins',confidence='low')
P('8-04','Polyhedral variants of the figure calculus',[{'cote':'156-8','scan':27,'file':'J156-8-04','lines':'82-98'}],'On devrait passer en revue les propositions pertinentes for the polyhedral theory.','Check restriction, local detection and gluing with ≪pol and polyhedral compatibility; distinguish the proved union criterion from the unperformed review.')
P('8-05','Equivalence of the final primitive axiom system',[{'cote':'156-8','scan':30,'file':'J156-8-04','lines':'174-207'},{'cote':'156-8','scan':31,'file':'J156-8-04','lines':'227-250'}],'Reformulate magasins using ≤, open refinement and interior disjointness; a lifting condition is tentatively proposed as an axiom.','The unique-carrier/lifting formulation can be checked formally, but full equivalence requires the same sibling-face disjointness hypothesis on both sides; resolve the scan before proving that version.')
